  "ailmentDescThunderblight": "Thunderblight is caused by the Thunder Element which increases the Hunter's chance of being stunned by Monster attacks.\nIt can be cured by consuming a Nulberry, or using a Cleanser Booster.",
  "ailmentDescWaterblight": "Waterblight is caused by the Water Element which reduces the Stamina recovery of the Hunter.\nIt can be cured by consuming a Nulberry, or using a Cleanser Booster.",
  "ailmentDescFireblight": "Fireblight is caused by the Fire Element which causes the hunter to lose health over time.\nIt can be cured by consuming a Nulberry. When available, players can jump into a nearby water, or roll 3 times on the ground.",
  "ailmentDescIceblight": "Iceblight is caused by the Ice Element which increases the Stamina consumption when performing tasks such as dashing, attacking, and dodging.\nIt can be cured by consuming a Nulberry.",
  "ailmentDescDragonblight": "Dragonblight is caused by the Dragon Element which nullifies the damaging effects and status buildup from this element.\nIt can be cured by consuming a Nulberry.",
  "ailmentDescBlast": "Blast is a status that marks a monster that can damage them through small explosions.\nIt can be cured with a Nulberry or by dodge-rolling up to three times.",
  "ailmentDescBlastblight": "Blastblight causes the target to explode after some time has passed, or upon receiving an impactful attack.\nIt can be cured with a Nulberry or by dodge-rolling up to three times.",
  "ailmentDescBleeding": "Bleeding causes the players to lose Health when performing actions such as moving, attacking, or dodging.\nIt can be cured by eating an Astera Jerky, Well-Done Steak, or Sushifish Scale, or by crouching for a few seconds.",
  "ailmentDescFrenzy": "Frenzy will cause the Hunter to temporarily receive more damage when fully infected.\nIt can be cured by using a Nulberry.",
  "ailmentDescFrostblight": "Frostblight prevents the hunter from moving or acting temporarily.\nIt can be cured with a Cleanser or by having a Bind Resistance Level 3.",
  "ailmentDescWebbed": "Webbed prevents the hunter from moving or acting temporarily.\nIt can be cured with a Cleanser, by moving, pressing buttons, being knocked by an attack, or taking a hit.",
  "ailmentDescPoison": "Poison gradually depletes the health of the target over time.\nThe Poison effect can be cured by Antidote, Herbal Medicine, or Herbal Powder.",
  "ailmentDescSleep": "Sleep causes the target to fall asleep which renders them susceptible to a one-time attack after.\nThe target will wake up after they receive damage.\nIt can be cured with an Energy Drink, being it by an ally or a Monster.",
  "ailmentDescParalysis": "Paralysis renders the hunter or monster immobilized and susceptible to increased damage for the duration.\nIt can be cured by impacts with large amounts of knockback, such as an upswing from a Hammer or Great Sword.",
